{title: Be Thou My Vision}
{artist: Irish, 8th c. · tr. Byrne}
{key: E}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
[E]Be thou my [B]vision, O [C#m]Lord of my [A]heart —
[E]naught be all [A]else to me [B]save that thou art:
[C#m]thou my best [A]thought, by [E]day or by [B]night,
[E]waking or [A]sleeping, thy [B]presence my [E]light.

Verse 2
[E]Be Thou my [B]Wisdom, and [C#m]Thou my true [A]Word; I
[E]ever with Thee [A]and Thou with [B]me, Lord; Thou my
[C#m]great Father, and [A]I Thy [E]true son; Thou [B]in
[E]me dwelling, [A]and I [B]with Thee [E]one.

Verse 3
[E]Be Thou my [B]battle Shield, [C#m]Sword for the [A]fight; Be
[E]Thou my Dignity, [A]Thou my [B]Delight; Thou my soul's
[C#m]Shelter, Thou my [A]high [E]Tower: Raise Thou [B]me
[E]heav'nward, O [A]Pow'r [B]of my [E]pow'r.

Verse 4
[E]Riches I [B]heed not, [C#m]nor man's [A]empty praise,
[E]Thou mine Inheritance, [A]now and [B]always: Thou and Thou
[C#m]only, be first [A]in [E]my heart, High [B]King
[E]of Heaven, [A]my [B]Treasure Thou [E]art.

Verse 5
[E]High King [B]of Heaven, [C#m]my victory [A]won, May
[E]I reach Heav'ns [A]joys, O [B]bright Heaven's Sun! Heart
[C#m]of my own [A]heart, [E]whatever befall, Still [B]be
[E]my Vision, [A]O [B]Ruler of [E]all.
